  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "subset",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/OT/Layout/GPOS/CursivePosFormat1.hh",
    "description": "CursivePosFormat1::subset maps retained source coverage glyphs with `glyph_map[p.first]` but does not reject `HB_MAP_VALUE_INVALID` when the old glyph has no old-to-new mapping. It then marks that iterator as sorting-preserving and passes the invalid value to Coverage serialization. With `g == UINT_MAX`, CoverageFormat2_4::serialize's sentinel initialization (`last = UINT_MAX-1`, `range = UINT_MAX`) treats the first glyph as contiguous, allocates zero ranges, and writes `rangeRecord.arrayZ[UINT_MAX].last`, producing the wild write observed at CoverageFormat2.hh:106. The primary missing validation is in the CursivePos subsetting caller; it should only serialize successfully mapped glyphs (or fail safely).",
    "conditions": "A crafted font must retain a GPOS CursivePosFormat1 coverage entry through `glyphset_gsub`, while that source glyph is absent from the subset plan's `glyph_map`. Map lookup then yields `HB_MAP_VALUE_INVALID` (0xFFFFFFFF). The CursivePos iterator must remain nonempty and reach coverage serialization; because the invalid mapped glyph is the first value, Coverage selects the medium format and its range-building sentinel arithmetic leaves the range index at UINT_MAX, causing the out-of-bounds write."
  },
